  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support of IOM Activities in Pakistan Outlines in the 2023 Refugee Response Plan (RRP) for the Afghanistan Situation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Instability in Afghanistan during the past few decades has led to a substantial influx of Afghans into Pakistan. In this project, IOM is seeking to expand its support to vulnerable Afghan nationals in Pakistan and host communities to enhance their living conditions and resilience. This is being achieved through a set of activities centred around facilitating Afghan nationals&apos; access to services through efforts to mitigate the tensions that might arise with the host community and through efforts targeting both the basic needs of targeted populations. For this, IOM&apos;s support evolves around the tracking the human mobility of Afghan nationals and efforts to comprehensively map their needs, and provide evidence-based cash assistance, housing support, health support, access to clean and safe water (Water, Hygiene and Sanitation (WASH)) and rehabilitation of community-based infrastructure.</narrative>
  </description>
